Hi all,

Tomorrow (Friday, 5/15) at 10am in Wickson 2124 Grace Charles will give a talk on structural equation modeling (SEM) in R. If you can't make it in person, check it out live online, here <https://plus.google.com/events/clu0tuh1d7vtj7inrucnf57j52s>. From Grace:

I'll give a presentation on structural equation models in R. Structural equation models are a way to estimate both direct and indirect connections among a set of variables. They're also visual, making them great way to link complex concepts and your data. I'll show some examples using the Lavaan package.

We will have the usual work session after the talk until 12. See you there,

Michael

