Hi Laura,

Could you provide a sample of the data frame (*before* these conversions) so that we can see what initial formats are?  The best way to do this is with the `dput()` command.  The following will print the first 10 lines of your data frame in an easy-to-transfer format:

    dput(Broiler[1:10,])

Copy and paste the output from that into your e-mail.

Also, our own Bonnie Dixon wrote a tremendously useful tutorial on handling dates and times: http://www.noamross.net/blog/2014/2/10/using-times-and-dates-in-r---presentation-code.html

